WEBVTT

00:08.500 --> 00:11.574
♪ But where are those good ol
d-fashioned values ♪

00:11.642 --> 00:14.548
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.616 --> 00:18.491
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.559 --> 00:21.298
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.366 --> 00:23.002
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.069 --> 00:24.372
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.439 --> 00:27.545
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.738 --> 00:39.944
Ah, it smells so good out here.

00:40.012 --> 00:41.179
You see, Peter?

00:41.246 --> 00:43.082
This is a much better way to spend a Sunday

00:43.150 --> 00:45.056
than what you dragged us to last week.

00:45.125 --> 00:46.693
Hey, if I'm starring in a production

00:46.761 --> 00:49.266
<i>of Starlight Express,
" I want my whole family there.</i>

00:49.334 --> 00:51.638
Starlight Express! Starlight Express!

00:51.706 --> 00:54.546
Starlight Express! Starlight Express!

00:54.614 --> 00:56.717
Starlight Express! Starlight Express!

00:56.786 --> 00:58.487
Starlight Express! Starlight Express!

00:58.555 --> 00:59.825
Starlight Express!

00:59.893 --> 01:01.462
Starlight Exprs!

01:01.530 --> 01:03.065
Starlight Express!

01:03.133 --> 01:04.971
Starlight Express!

01:05.039 --> 01:07.344
Starlight Express!

01:07.411 --> 01:08.679
Starlight Express!

01:10.085 --> 01:11.052
Starlight Express.

01:16.333 --> 01:17.602
Stewie, look.

01:17.670 --> 01:19.005
A butterfly.

01:20.544 --> 01:22.046
Let's get it!

01:23.716 --> 01:26.055
Uh, Chris, I don't think we
should be leaving the trail.

01:28.030 --> 01:29.665
: I shall put you in a glass box

01:29.732 --> 01:31.402
to display on Saint Trimmings Day.

01:31.469 --> 01:32.739
Awww.

01:32.808 --> 01:35.212
British guys always capture my butterflies.

01:35.280 --> 01:37.318
Yes, and to add insult to injury,

01:37.385 --> 01:38.987
I shall present to you my fanny:

01:39.055 --> 01:40.759
Sir Chadwell Heath.

01:44.436 --> 01:45.705
Aw, darn it.

01:45.772 --> 01:48.577
Hey, wait a second. Where are we?

01:48.645 --> 01:50.683
Oh, no.

01:50.751 --> 01:51.852
Hey, Chris, did you know

01:51.921 --> 01:54.157
your bacne spells "Citibank" in Braille?

01:58.169 --> 02:01.108
Great. You had to chase the butterfly.

02:01.175 --> 02:03.647
Yes, I had to chase the butterfly.

02:03.715 --> 02:05.453
I came out here to observe nature.

02:05.521 --> 02:07.056
What did you come out here for?

02:07.124 --> 02:09.729
I came to the woods because I
wished to live deliberately,

02:09.797 --> 02:12.135
and see if I could not
learn what it had to teach,

02:12.203 --> 02:14.073
and not, when I came to die,

02:14.141 --> 02:16.412
discover that I had not lived.

02:16.479 --> 02:18.619
Wow, Stewie. That was beautiful.

02:18.686 --> 02:20.389
Did you write that? No.

02:20.458 --> 02:22.160
But can you tell me who did?

02:22.227 --> 02:24.064
Log on now.

02:27.441 --> 02:29.277
All right, let's tally up those responses.

02:31.818 --> 02:33.153
Wow.

02:33.222 --> 02:35.057
You know who that is?
You know who Thornton Mellon--

02:35.126 --> 02:36.329
First of all, it was Henry David Thoreau.

02:36.397 --> 02:37.998
But do you know who Thornton Mellon is?

02:38.066 --> 02:41.141
<i>That was Rodney Dangerfield's character in
Back to School.</i>

02:41.209 --> 02:43.680
You feel good about yourselves? Huh?

02:43.748 --> 02:46.220
This is why the other countries
are beating us, you know!

02:46.287 --> 02:48.023
So you know, you got only yourself to blame

02:48.091 --> 02:49.626
next time you go to the vet and complain

02:49.694 --> 02:52.333
that that Indian doctor is
too rough with your cat.

02:55.041 --> 02:58.215
Stewie, are we gonna die?

02:58.283 --> 02:59.919
Hey, hey.

02:59.987 --> 03:01.157
Probably.

03:01.223 --> 03:03.495
I-I don't want to die!

03:03.563 --> 03:05.432
You know, Chris, if by some miracle,

03:05.501 --> 03:07.303
we do manage to get out of here alive,

03:07.372 --> 03:09.676
I'm gonna finally run
for public office again.

03:09.744 --> 03:12.015
I think people have forgotten
my last embarrassment.

03:15.024 --> 03:17.093
Harry Truman. Stupid jerk.

03:17.162 --> 03:19.201
Freakin' FDR's ass bitch.

03:19.268 --> 03:20.971
If we get back home alive,

03:21.039 --> 03:23.778
I'm gonna finally open up
to Ellen from my math class

03:23.845 --> 03:25.481
and tell her homuch I like her.

03:25.549 --> 03:27.386
I'd like those things for us, Chris.

03:29.659 --> 03:30.761
What are you doing?

03:30.829 --> 03:32.032
I'm digging a hole.

03:32.100 --> 03:33.301
Why?

03:33.369 --> 03:35.104
'Cause I like to sleep on my side.

03:42.658 --> 03:45.364
Our top story: The search for two local boys

03:45.431 --> 03:47.468
lost in the woods drags
on into its third day.

03:47.536 --> 03:48.740
That's right, Diane.

03:48.807 --> 03:50.978
Still no sign of Chris and Stewie Griffin.

03:51.046 --> 03:52.849
Here's the update from the local authorities

03:52.916 --> 03:54.755
who are overseeing the
search party's efforts.

03:54.822 --> 03:57.461
We're still very optimistic that
we're gonna find these kids,

03:57.527 --> 03:59.999
and we just want to urge
everyone not to give up hope.

04:00.067 --> 04:01.369
All right, everyone,

04:01.438 --> 04:03.776
we are officially looking for corpses.

04:03.843 --> 04:05.813
Repeat, this is now a recovery effort.

04:05.881 --> 04:07.819
We are officially looking for corpses,

04:07.887 --> 04:09.056
so let's get back out there,

04:09.123 --> 04:10.725
bring back those dead bodies.

04:10.793 --> 04:12.264
Oh, God, this is horrible!

04:12.333 --> 04:13.766
I can't watch anymore!

04:13.835 --> 04:16.106
Mom, Daddy, thank you
so much for coming over.

04:16.174 --> 04:17.677
Oh, of course, dear.

04:17.743 --> 04:18.913
I don't know what to do.

04:18.980 --> 04:20.482
They scoured the area,

04:20.550 --> 04:21.887
and there's no sign of them.

04:21.955 --> 04:23.858
I feel like I can't just
sit here doing nothing,

04:23.926 --> 04:25.595
but I don't know what I can do.

04:25.663 --> 04:27.401
I'll tell you who could help. Medium.

04:27.469 --> 04:28.938
Daddy, that's not a real person.

04:29.005 --> 04:30.607
That's a character on a TV show.

04:30.675 --> 04:32.346
Don't you disparage Medium.

04:32.414 --> 04:33.816
Medium works very hard.

04:33.884 --> 04:35.920
You know, Mom, I saw this
thing on the Discovery Channel

04:35.989 --> 04:38.025
about psychics who help
find people who are lost.

04:38.093 --> 04:39.195
Really?

04:39.263 --> 04:40.565
I saw this thing on the Discovery Channel

04:40.633 --> 04:42.538
about this fat woman who sat on her dog

04:42.606 --> 04:44.375
and it went up inside her guts.

04:47.719 --> 04:49.120
It's been three days,

04:49.188 --> 04:50.923
and I just don't know where else to turn.

04:50.992 --> 04:52.663
Please, can you help me?

04:52.731 --> 04:54.099
Don't worry, Lois.

04:54.167 --> 04:57.073
The spirit world wants
very much to assist you.

04:58.276 --> 05:00.682
Your missing sons will be found.

05:00.749 --> 05:04.592
Oh, oh! Thank you, thank you so much!

05:04.660 --> 05:06.797
I can't tell you how reassuring that is.

05:06.865 --> 05:10.139
Ah. My babies are okay.

05:12.244 --> 05:14.114
Will you answer one question for me?

05:14.182 --> 05:15.251
Yes.

05:15.319 --> 05:17.657
Thank you so much.

05:22.436 --> 05:25.744
Well, Stewie, I think we're finished.

05:25.812 --> 05:28.083
It sure looks that way.

05:28.151 --> 05:30.656
It's been a pleasure
serving with you, Chris.

05:30.724 --> 05:33.062
And with you, Stewie.

05:33.130 --> 05:35.166
Jeffrey! Jeffrey, come back.

05:35.234 --> 05:36.937
It's gonna get dark soon!

05:37.005 --> 05:39.309
All this drama over a turkey burger?!

05:40.549 --> 05:42.183
Oh, thank God!

05:42.251 --> 05:43.320
Oh, you're not Jeffrey.

05:43.388 --> 05:45.158
You're that missing baby and boy.

05:45.226 --> 05:46.493
Jeffrey!

05:46.562 --> 05:48.767
I found that missing baby and boy!

05:48.833 --> 05:50.504
I don't care.

05:52.544 --> 05:53.780
Mommy!

05:53.845 --> 05:55.049
Chris! Stewie!

05:55.116 --> 05:56.551
My babies!

05:56.619 --> 05:59.058
Oh, I'm so happy you're safe!

05:59.125 --> 06:00.762
Oh, I knew they'd find you.

06:00.831 --> 06:02.399
I knew you were okay.

06:02.467 --> 06:03.970
It's just like the psychic said.

06:04.037 --> 06:06.243
Thank you all for your help, everybody.

06:06.311 --> 06:07.546
Oh, for definite.

06:07.614 --> 06:09.851
It's just like a childhood
game of Hide and Find!

06:09.919 --> 06:11.089
You said it, friend!

06:11.156 --> 06:12.424
What do you say for celebration

06:12.492 --> 06:14.260
we go dunk our whistles in the trough?

06:14.329 --> 06:16.734
Ah! We should totally phone Gaspard!

06:16.801 --> 06:18.540
Ah! He would love to hear this tale!

06:18.608 --> 06:21.980
Oh, but I only have 15
pfenigs on my phone card.

06:22.048 --> 06:24.386
Happy Gerbitz Day.

06:24.454 --> 06:25.523
Ah! Ah! Ah!

06:25.592 --> 06:26.859
Ah! Ah!

06:31.502 --> 06:35.243
Oh, it is so good to have my
boys back home safe and sound.

06:35.310 --> 06:36.913
Thank God for that psychic.

06:36.981 --> 06:38.819
What are you talking about?
The psychic didn't do anything.

06:38.887 --> 06:41.291
Well, she said we were
gonna find them and we did.

06:41.360 --> 06:43.195
I always wondered about psychics,

06:43.264 --> 06:45.267
but I gotta tell ya, I'm a believer now.

06:45.334 --> 06:48.108
Yeah, I'm gonna go back and
see what else she has to say.

06:48.176 --> 06:50.312
Hey, check it out. Chris and Stewie,

06:50.381 --> 06:52.551
you're on the front page of the paper.

06:52.619 --> 06:54.492
You know, Chris, that girl from school

06:54.560 --> 06:56.328
sees that picture and you're in.

06:56.397 --> 06:58.300
Look, Stewie, I'm not
really gonna ask her out.

06:58.367 --> 07:01.173
I think that just might
have been cocky forest talk.

07:01.242 --> 07:02.576
No, but you got to take advantage of this.

07:02.643 --> 07:03.780
Seize your moment.

07:03.849 --> 07:05.752
Like the Duck Founding Father.

07:05.819 --> 07:08.525
Gentlemen, these are all
important fundamental rights,

07:08.593 --> 07:11.833
but I move we strike the
right to bob for small fish

07:11.901 --> 07:13.604
with your butt in the air. All in favor?

07:13.672 --> 07:14.540
Aye.

07:14.608 --> 07:15.542
Opposed?

07:16.679 --> 07:17.713
The motion carries.

07:20.455 --> 07:22.759
I don't know about this, Stewie.

07:22.827 --> 07:24.264
Nonsense. You're a hero now.

07:24.331 --> 07:25.432
Your picture's in the paper.

07:25.500 --> 07:26.569
She'll be fawning all over you.

07:26.637 --> 07:27.571
Now, which one is she?

07:27.639 --> 07:29.510
There.

07:32.452 --> 07:34.422
Hi, Chris!

07:34.490 --> 07:36.293
Wait a minute. That's the girl?

07:36.360 --> 07:38.665
Yeah. Isn't she special?

07:38.732 --> 07:40.535
That's the way the state of
Rhode Island would put it.

07:40.603 --> 07:43.878
Uh, there's something...
up with her, isn't there?

07:43.946 --> 07:45.615
Yeah. She's got Down's Syndrome.

07:45.683 --> 07:46.886
Oh, okay, well, there we go.

07:46.954 --> 07:48.422
She's so sweet.

07:48.489 --> 07:51.296
And doesn't she have the
most beautiful eyes?

07:51.364 --> 07:53.067
Well, the spacing seems a tad off,

07:53.134 --> 07:54.571
but, yeah, individually, they're not awful.

07:54.639 --> 07:56.141
All right, I'm on board. Go talk to her.

07:57.346 --> 07:59.851
Um, hi, Ellen.

07:59.919 --> 08:01.187
Hi, Chris.

08:01.255 --> 08:03.760
Um, this is my little brother Stewie.

08:03.827 --> 08:06.634
Your head makes me laugh.

08:06.701 --> 08:09.708
I'm guessing this one owned a bunny,
but not anymore.

08:11.279 --> 08:13.951
Um, listen there's something
I've wanted to tell you

08:14.019 --> 08:15.788
for a really long time.

08:15.856 --> 08:17.327
Oh, yeah? What?

08:17.395 --> 08:19.900
Well, um, I really like you.

08:21.304 --> 08:23.541
And I was wondering if maybe, um...

08:23.609 --> 08:25.645
you want to go out on a date with me.

08:25.714 --> 08:28.353
Okay. Pick me up Saturday at 8:00.

08:28.421 --> 08:30.492
Great. See you then.

08:30.561 --> 08:32.731
There you go. Being confident.

08:32.799 --> 08:35.770
Like an Italian guy in any
given theoretical situation.

08:35.839 --> 08:37.241
If that was me...

08:37.309 --> 08:39.214
<i>I'm, I'm just saying,
if that was me...</i>

08:39.282 --> 08:41.453
<i>They are lucky that was not me.</i>

08:41.520 --> 08:43.457
Because, if the circumstances were such,

08:43.524 --> 08:45.195
as you have described them,

08:45.263 --> 08:46.365
<i>but with me in them,</i>

08:46.432 --> 08:48.737
that's a very different and scary outcome

08:48.804 --> 08:50.007
for those involved.

08:50.074 --> 08:51.276
If.

08:54.551 --> 08:55.789
Oh, my God, Brian.

08:55.857 --> 08:57.157
Oh... my... God.

08:57.226 --> 08:58.261
Whoa. What is it? What happened?

08:58.329 --> 08:59.797
I just went to see my psychic Estelle,

08:59.866 --> 09:02.069
and she told me that Stewie is gonna grow up

09:02.138 --> 09:03.773
to be very successful.

09:03.840 --> 09:05.412
Ah! Isn't that great news?

09:05.480 --> 09:07.282
You went to see that psychic again?

09:07.351 --> 09:08.318
That's the third time this week.

09:08.386 --> 09:10.290
She's a lifesaver, Brian.

09:10.359 --> 09:12.630
She gives me the confidence to live my life

09:12.697 --> 09:14.433
knowing I'm making the right choices.

09:14.501 --> 09:16.671
Wow, and she does all this for free?

09:16.740 --> 09:18.243
No, she charges me.

09:18.311 --> 09:20.582
She charges you?! Well, that's weird.

09:20.650 --> 09:23.657
Why would you pay her to
hear things you want to hear?

09:23.724 --> 09:25.895
I'm not crazy about your tone, Brian.

09:25.963 --> 09:28.167
Well, I just think you're
being taken for a ride, Lois.

09:28.235 --> 09:29.971
Like a snail on the back of a turtle.

09:31.910 --> 09:33.314
Slow down!

09:33.381 --> 09:35.987
I want to get there,
but I want to get there alive!

09:38.695 --> 09:41.300
Mom, why do I have to
take a bath with Stewie?

09:41.368 --> 09:44.039
Because, Meg, Estelle told
me that someone in the family

09:44.105 --> 09:45.644
was in danger of drowning,

09:45.712 --> 09:47.815
and that I should take
some steps to prevent it.

09:47.883 --> 09:56.671
So, from now on, everybody has a bath buddy.

10:03.923 --> 10:05.524
What am I gonna do?

10:05.593 --> 10:08.365
I'm really nervous about
my date with Ellen tonight.

10:08.433 --> 10:12.309
I mean, I want to impress her,
but what if I mess things up?

10:12.376 --> 10:13.880
Oh, come on, Chris, it's just a matter

10:13.948 --> 10:15.181
of getting off on the right foot.

10:15.249 --> 10:18.357
First things first.
Let's get you looking sharp.

10:22.066 --> 10:24.138
♪ You've got to look your best tonight ♪

10:24.206 --> 10:25.976
♪ You tubby little parasite ♪

10:26.043 --> 10:29.517
♪ 'Cause there's a lovely lady
and she's waiting for you ♪

10:29.586 --> 10:31.322
♪ And though her pretty face may seem ♪

10:31.390 --> 10:33.293
♪ A special person's wettest dream ♪

10:33.362 --> 10:36.902
♪ Before you get to see it
there are things you must do ♪

10:36.970 --> 10:40.377
♪ We'll try a tie and
boutonniere of yellow ♪

10:40.445 --> 10:44.288
♪ Or a rose that shows that
you're a classy fellow ♪

10:44.355 --> 10:48.363
♪ With the posh panache of
Jefferson at Monticello ♪

10:48.431 --> 10:51.538
♪ Busting out a mile with style ♪

10:51.606 --> 10:53.643
♪ I know you just can't wait to stare ♪

10:53.711 --> 10:55.446
♪ At all that luscious orange hair ♪

10:55.515 --> 10:58.990
♪ But, boy, before you touch a single curl ♪

10:59.058 --> 11:01.998
♪ You must impress that ultra
boomin', all consumin' ♪

11:02.066 --> 11:06.475
♪ Poorly groomin' Down's Syndrome girl ♪

11:08.280 --> 11:10.283
♪ On any normal day you reek ♪

11:10.351 --> 11:12.122
♪ As if you're on a farting streak ♪

11:12.190 --> 11:15.731
♪ Your finger's up your nose and
you are dripping with drool ♪

11:15.798 --> 11:17.636
♪ But if you want a lady's love ♪

11:17.702 --> 11:19.507
♪ You're better off by smelling of ♪

11:19.575 --> 11:22.981
♪ A gentleman's cologne instead
of sneakers and stool ♪

11:23.049 --> 11:24.787
♪ A squirt, a spurt ♪

11:24.855 --> 11:26.758
♪ Of somethin' just for Ellen ♪

11:26.825 --> 11:30.167
♪ And you'll see that she
will find you so compellin' ♪

11:30.235 --> 11:32.104
♪ And she does because ♪

11:32.172 --> 11:34.544
♪ The only smell that she'll be smellin' ♪

11:34.612 --> 11:36.581
♪ Won't be coming from your bum ♪

11:38.019 --> 11:39.723
♪ You wanna take that little whore ♪

11:39.792 --> 11:41.761
♪ And spin her on the dancing floor ♪

11:41.829 --> 11:45.404
♪ But boy, before you do a single twirl ♪

11:45.472 --> 11:47.376
♪ You must impress that effervescing ♪

11:47.444 --> 11:49.112
♪ Self-possessing, no BS-ing ♪

11:49.181 --> 11:52.822
♪ Down's Syndrome girl ♪

11:58.670 --> 12:02.579
♪ Her eyes are emerald portals ♪

12:02.647 --> 12:05.152
♪ To a secret land of love ♪

12:05.220 --> 12:10.831
♪ And her smile is like the
sweetest summer flower ♪

12:12.505 --> 12:15.911
♪ Her kiss is so inviting ♪

12:15.979 --> 12:20.990
♪ And her hugs are so delighting ♪

12:21.057 --> 12:22.427
♪ And what makes them really nice ♪

12:22.495 --> 12:23.763
♪ Is that they've got a little spice ♪

12:23.831 --> 12:25.335
♪ Because they're tighter than a vice ♪

12:25.403 --> 12:28.242
♪ And they go on for an hour ♪

13:03.196 --> 13:04.965
♪ My boy, between the two of us ♪

13:05.033 --> 13:07.136
♪ We'll get you on that shorty bus ♪

13:07.204 --> 13:10.479
♪ And then you're gonna
take it for a whirl ♪

13:10.546 --> 13:12.484
♪ Now go impress that super-thrilling ♪

13:12.551 --> 13:14.186
♪ Wish-fulfilling, Yoohoo-spilling ♪

13:14.254 --> 13:15.859
♪ Ultra-swinging, boner-bringing ♪

13:15.926 --> 13:17.194
♪ Gaily singing, dingalinging ♪

13:17.262 --> 13:19.165
♪ Stupefying, fortifying ♪

13:19.234 --> 13:20.504
♪ As of Monday, shoelace tying ♪

13:20.571 --> 13:21.973
♪ Stimulating, titillating ♪

13:22.041 --> 13:23.343
♪ Kitty cat impersonating ♪

13:23.412 --> 13:25.081
♪ Mega-rocking, pillow-talking ♪

13:25.149 --> 13:26.352
♪ Just a little crooked walking ♪

13:26.420 --> 13:27.621
♪ Coyly pouting, booby-sprouting ♪

13:27.689 --> 13:28.589
♪ For some reason always shouting ♪

13:28.658 --> 13:29.591
♪ Fascinating, captivating ♪

13:29.659 --> 13:33.301
♪ Happiness and joy creating ♪

13:34.305 --> 13:37.645
♪ Down's Syndrome girl! ♪

13:41.423 --> 13:43.593
Okay, Brian, I'm here.

13:43.662 --> 13:45.130
Now, what is it you want?

13:45.198 --> 13:46.802
All right, look, Lois, this psychic nonsense

13:46.869 --> 13:49.207
has gone too far,
so I'm going to prove to you

13:49.275 --> 13:51.813
that there is no such thing
as someone who is psychic,

13:51.882 --> 13:53.518
and that with the most minimal training

13:53.586 --> 13:54.920
and the right set of buzzwords,

13:54.988 --> 13:56.692
anyone can appear to be psychic.

13:56.761 --> 13:58.964
Even a complete boob like Peter. Watch this.

13:59.032 --> 14:00.802
Excuse me, ma'am. I'm psychic,

14:00.870 --> 14:03.007
and I'm getting a strong feeling from you.

14:03.075 --> 14:06.047
Do you have a watch or
clock that no longer works?

14:06.115 --> 14:09.055
W-Wow. I used to have a watch that broke.

14:09.123 --> 14:11.294
You see, just by asking
very general questions

14:11.362 --> 14:12.764
that would apply to most people,

14:12.832 --> 14:15.838
a person can appear to have
inside knowledge about you.

14:15.907 --> 14:18.244
I'm also sensing that you
have a dead relative.

14:18.312 --> 14:20.182
My husband died of cancer last year.

14:20.249 --> 14:21.386
Oh, my God. Awesome.

14:21.453 --> 14:23.356
Okay, uh, I'm sensing some other bad stuff.

14:23.425 --> 14:25.729
My daughter was just in an accident.

14:25.797 --> 14:27.134
Sweet! High five! You're awful.

14:27.203 --> 14:28.704
Hey, you don't want to hear the truth,

14:28.772 --> 14:29.773
don't come to the park.

14:29.842 --> 14:31.411
Okay.

14:31.478 --> 14:32.913
Okay, you made your point.

14:32.981 --> 14:33.984
I get it.

14:34.052 --> 14:35.620
Maybe I went a little overboard

14:35.688 --> 14:37.225
with the things Estelle told me.

14:37.292 --> 14:39.330
All right, look, can we just go home now?

14:39.397 --> 14:40.665
Come on, Peter, let's go.

14:40.734 --> 14:42.670
Brian, I felt something.

14:42.738 --> 14:45.244
Just now, talking to
that bitch cancer widow.

14:45.311 --> 14:47.416
I think I may have a gift.

14:47.485 --> 14:49.388
Peter, we were just doing a demonstration.

14:49.456 --> 14:50.958
No, Brian. This is real.

14:51.026 --> 14:53.264
I believe I am psychic.

14:53.331 --> 14:54.835
My first prediction:

14:54.903 --> 14:57.676
I am either going to fly or
ruin that family's picnic.

14:59.179 --> 15:01.016
Hey! You've ruined our picnic!

15:01.083 --> 15:02.655
Psychic.

15:09.207 --> 15:10.043
Peter, what are you doing?

15:10.111 --> 15:11.111
Quiet, Brian.

15:11.179 --> 15:13.015
I'm performing a psychic reading.

15:13.082 --> 15:15.188
Peter, for the last time,
you're not psychic.

15:15.256 --> 15:16.859
I most certainly am.

15:16.927 --> 15:18.395
All right, Quagmire, clear your mi...

15:18.462 --> 15:19.566
Ooh, soft hands.

15:19.633 --> 15:20.800
Clear your mind,

15:20.869 --> 15:23.074
remove all traces of unease and doubt,

15:23.141 --> 15:25.880
and I will tell you your future.

15:25.948 --> 15:27.217
What is it, Peter?

15:27.285 --> 15:28.955
You will die in a plane crash

15:29.022 --> 15:31.193
and be reincarnated as a prophylactic.

15:33.333 --> 15:34.568
All right!

15:34.636 --> 15:36.340
No, no, not all right!

15:39.414 --> 15:41.785
Well, I'm glad we're
finally going out, Ellen.

15:41.853 --> 15:44.259
I've really liked you for a long time.

15:44.326 --> 15:46.363
Hey, what the hell you think you're doing?

15:46.431 --> 15:47.568
Sitting down.

15:47.636 --> 15:49.505
Get up and pull my chair out for me.

15:49.573 --> 15:51.409
Oh, goodness, I'm sorry.

15:51.477 --> 15:53.048
I'm so sorry.

15:53.115 --> 15:54.317
That's better.

15:55.621 --> 15:58.093
You going to be this rude all evening?

15:58.161 --> 16:00.767
You haven't asked me anything about myself.

16:00.834 --> 16:02.671
Oh. Um, sorry.

16:02.738 --> 16:04.910
Um, uh, so... so, what do your parents do?

16:04.978 --> 16:06.013
That's better.

16:06.081 --> 16:07.416
My dad's an accountant,

16:07.483 --> 16:10.323
and my mom is the former governor of Alaska.

16:10.391 --> 16:11.559
Oh, that's cool.

16:11.627 --> 16:12.796
It's real cool.

16:12.863 --> 16:14.733
Now, get up, come over here,

16:14.801 --> 16:16.571
and give me a shoulder massage.

16:16.639 --> 16:18.277
Okay.

16:18.345 --> 16:21.184
Boy, you're tougher than a doggy dominatrix.

16:21.251 --> 16:22.586
Do it, do it. Come on, do it.

16:22.654 --> 16:24.023
Do it, do it.

16:24.090 --> 16:26.297
Aah, yes!

16:26.363 --> 16:28.401
Yes! Aah, you bitch!

16:28.470 --> 16:29.737
Aah!

16:35.252 --> 16:36.619
Oh, my God, this is awful.

16:36.688 --> 16:38.392
There's got to be 200 people here.

16:44.340 --> 16:45.376
Thank you.

16:45.444 --> 16:46.744
Thank you so much for coming.

16:46.813 --> 16:48.316
Thank... Hold on.

16:48.384 --> 16:50.020
I'm sensing something psychic.

16:50.088 --> 16:52.493
Ma'am, did you have a female relative

16:52.561 --> 16:54.296
who's passed on to the other side

16:54.365 --> 16:56.769
named, um, um...

16:56.837 --> 16:58.608
Polly? Polly! I said it first.

16:58.676 --> 17:00.780
That was amazing.

17:00.848 --> 17:02.851
I've never seen a bad show at the Marriott.

17:02.919 --> 17:06.160
Oh, myod, they're all
falling for this insanity.

17:06.228 --> 17:07.529
I'm sensing a black guy over here.

17:07.597 --> 17:08.532
Is there a black guy?

17:08.601 --> 17:10.136
Me! I'm a black guy.

17:11.875 --> 17:13.110
Yes, good, good.

17:13.178 --> 17:15.649
I'm sensing your infant
daughter has earrings.

17:15.718 --> 17:17.286
He's right. She does.

17:19.193 --> 17:20.997
Peter, you got to stop this right now.

17:21.065 --> 17:22.165
Shut up, Lois.

17:22.233 --> 17:23.604
Don't mess up my psychic-ness.

17:23.670 --> 17:25.005
I'm sensing a doctor in the audience.

17:25.073 --> 17:26.309
Where is the doctor?

17:26.377 --> 17:27.411
I'm a doctor.

17:27.479 --> 17:28.916
Okay. Your great grandmother

17:28.984 --> 17:30.920
is contacting me right now,
and she wants to know

17:30.988 --> 17:33.059
if this rash looks like
it's going to go away.

17:33.127 --> 17:36.368
Well I-I-I guess I'd
tell her to use Bactine.

17:36.435 --> 17:38.438
No! She says Bactine hurts.

17:38.506 --> 17:40.309
She wants something more soothin

17:41.782 --> 17:43.752
Peter, we need your help.

17:43.819 --> 17:45.455
We just got word of a kidnap victim

17:45.523 --> 17:47.694
buried alive with a bomb
strapped to his chest.

17:47.762 --> 17:49.466
We need your psychic powers

17:49.535 --> 17:51.873
to lead us to him before the bomb goes off.

17:51.941 --> 17:53.074
Well, well.

17:53.142 --> 17:55.346
Finally, a true test of my abilities.

17:55.414 --> 17:56.885
You came to the right place, Joe.

17:56.953 --> 17:58.589
I'll psych that guy out for you.

17:58.656 --> 17:59.925
Peter, you can't do this.

17:59.991 --> 18:01.563
All right, I mean, it-it's one thing

18:01.631 --> 18:03.132
to take money from a bunch of suckers,

18:03.200 --> 18:04.235
but this is serious.

18:04.303 --> 18:05.739
You're a fraud. I am not.

18:05.807 --> 18:08.011
I'll tell you who's a fraud: Mr. Spock.

18:08.079 --> 18:10.283
Mr. Sulu, set a course for...
One moment, Captain.

18:10.351 --> 18:12.390
They're about to announce
the winning numbers

18:12.458 --> 18:13.926
for the Intergalactic Lottery.

18:13.994 --> 18:15.295
FEMALE VOICE: Today's winning numbers

18:15.363 --> 18:19.439
are 18, 24, 41 and 72.

18:19.507 --> 18:21.812
Ah, yes!

18:21.880 --> 18:23.048
You're damn right!

18:23.116 --> 18:24.118
Hell, yeah!

18:24.185 --> 18:25.353
You can suck it.

18:25.421 --> 18:27.192
You can suck it. You can suck it.

18:27.260 --> 18:28.795
You can all suck it!

18:28.863 --> 18:30.432
Live long and suck it!

18:32.872 --> 18:34.142
Well, Ellen, I had

18:34.210 --> 18:36.280
a really interesting time with you tonight.

18:36.348 --> 18:38.285
I guess I'll talk to you soon.

18:38.353 --> 18:39.791
You're not leaving yet.

18:39.857 --> 18:43.029
I need somebody to make
me an ice cream sundae,

18:43.097 --> 18:44.702
so get in the house.

18:44.769 --> 18:46.238
Okay, okay.

18:49.648 --> 18:52.086
Uh, unless you're going to pull a sundae

18:52.153 --> 18:53.656
out of your belly button,

18:53.725 --> 18:56.464
I'd get your ass in the kitchen.

18:56.530 --> 18:57.800
Oh, boy.

18:57.869 --> 19:00.073
My dogs are mooing today.

19:01.276 --> 19:03.447
No, no, no, no, no, no.

19:03.515 --> 19:04.584
What's the matter?

19:04.651 --> 19:06.755
Did I say put chocolate sauce on there?

19:06.823 --> 19:09.830
Did you hear me say put
chocolate sauce on there?

19:09.898 --> 19:11.198
Well, I... I just thought that...

19:11.266 --> 19:12.436
You thought what?

19:12.505 --> 19:14.909
You know, if you want access to this temple,

19:14.977 --> 19:17.248
you better pay the proper tribute.

19:17.315 --> 19:19.118
All right, that is it!

19:19.186 --> 19:21.123
I don't care how hot you are.

19:21.191 --> 19:23.763
I don't much like being treated this way.

19:23.831 --> 19:26.436
You know, I used to hear that
people with Down's syndrome

19:26.504 --> 19:28.507
were different than the rest of us,
but you're not.

19:28.575 --> 19:30.113
You're not different at all.

19:30.181 --> 19:33.254
You're just a bunch of like everyone else!

19:33.322 --> 19:35.526
I got bad news for you, buddy.

19:35.594 --> 19:37.029
You just blew it.

19:37.096 --> 19:39.168
Get out of my house now!

19:44.481 --> 19:45.618
How'd it go?

19:45.686 --> 19:47.655
Looks like I totally screwed that up.

19:47.723 --> 19:49.292
No, you didn't. You made a vow

19:49.360 --> 19:51.497
that you were going to ask
Ellen out, and you did.

19:51.565 --> 19:53.036
That took courage, my friend.

19:53.104 --> 19:55.007
Especially for a poor, timid sap like you.

19:55.075 --> 19:56.177
I'm proud of you.

19:56.245 --> 19:57.647
Thanks, Stewie.

19:57.715 --> 19:59.986
I'm just sorry I never
got to make out with her.

20:00.053 --> 20:02.157
Oh, she would have crushed
your scrote into a diamond

20:02.225 --> 20:03.427
with her robot-strength hand.

20:03.496 --> 20:05.567
Come on, let's get out of here.

20:07.438 --> 20:09.040
All right, Peter, we know the victim

20:09.108 --> 20:10.378
is somewhere in this area.

20:10.445 --> 20:12.316
We don't have much time before the bomb...

20:12.384 --> 20:13.486
Shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.

20:13.553 --> 20:14.923
Okay, Joe, when I'm tracking someone,

20:14.990 --> 20:16.360
it often helps to touch something

20:16.428 --> 20:17.396
that belongs to the victim.

20:17.463 --> 20:18.498
Does he have a wife?

20:18.566 --> 20:20.035
Uh, yeah.

20:22.174 --> 20:23.577
Yeah, uh-huh.

20:23.645 --> 20:26.217
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

20:26.285 --> 20:27.385
It's still very fuzzy.

20:27.453 --> 20:29.724
Does he have a daughter?

20:29.793 --> 20:31.163
Yeah, I see.

20:31.230 --> 20:33.000
Does he have maybe, like,
a thinner, hotter daughter?

20:33.068 --> 20:34.670
Well, yes, but she's only 12.

20:34.738 --> 20:36.176
Okay. Like-like a... like a young 12

20:36.243 --> 20:38.280
or, like, a "she eats a lot of milk products

20:38.348 --> 20:39.682
so she got her boobs early" 12?

20:39.750 --> 20:41.054
Which is a real thing, by the way.

20:41.122 --> 20:42.456
Peter, we're running out of time!

20:42.523 --> 20:43.960
All right, all right,
we'll try something else.

20:44.028 --> 20:48.171
I will now use my psychic
powers to seek help from beyond.

20:48.239 --> 20:51.144
I shall now channel the
ghost of Lou Costello,

20:51.213 --> 20:53.150
who will guide us to this soul in distress.

20:54.955 --> 20:56.425
Hi, everybody. It's me, Lou Costello.

20:56.493 --> 20:58.629
All right, what's the name
of the guy we're looking for?

20:58.698 --> 21:00.166
Well, he's an Asian fella-- Melvin Hu.

21:00.235 --> 21:01.570
That's what I want to find out. What?

21:01.638 --> 21:02.806
The name of the guy. Melvin Hu.

21:02.874 --> 21:03.909
Are you a cop? Yeah.

21:03.978 --> 21:05.178
You handling this case? Yeah.

21:05.246 --> 21:06.382
Then, what's the name of the guy? Hu.

21:06.450 --> 21:07.418
The guy we're looking for. Hu.

21:07.485 --> 21:08.454
The guy who's buried. Hu.

21:08.522 --> 21:09.723
The guy with the bomb. Hu.

21:09.791 --> 21:10.458
What street's he live on? First.

21:13.500 --> 21:14.736
Yeah, I'm not psychic.

21:14.737 --> 22:15.737
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru